{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1024","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1024","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1024\",\"parent_revision\":\"bbe07d415e7e6213150957c5abc7a3577e54b6c8d1c43f5f3e43273a5b86d26b\",\"root_revision\":\"bbe07d415e7e6213150957c5abc7a3577e54b6c8d1c43f5f3e43273a5b86d26b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-04-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe pre-tool-diagnostic-command-gate.cjs hook in orchestrator-discipline matches diagnostic command patterns (ruff check, ty check, pytest, prek run) anywhere in the Bash command string \u2014 including inside quoted arguments. This produces false positives when spawning kage-bunshin sessions whose prompts mention diagnostic commands. Example: `uv run spawn.py spawn --name x \\\"run ruff check on foo\\\"` triggers the warning because \\\"ruff check\\\" appears in the quoted prompt. The hook should extract the actual executable command and only match against that, not quoted string arguments.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-23T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-23T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **diagnostic-command-gate hook matches commands inside quoted strings (false positives)** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-23 \u2014 observed 3 false positives during kage-bunshin spawning\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe `matchesDiagnosticCommand` function receives only the portion of the command string that represents the actual executable invocation \u2014 the shell command stripped of its quoted string arguments. Diagnostic pattern regexes are applied to this stripped form only.\\n\\nThe stripping must handle:\\n- Single-quoted strings: `'...'`\\n- Double-quoted strings: `\\\"...\\\"`\\n- Nested or escaped quotes are not required to be handled (the existing hook is non-blocking and non-exhaustive, so approximate stripping is sufficient)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run spawn.py spawn --name x 'run ruff check on foo'` \u2014 hook produces NO warning (false positive eliminated)\\n2. `uv run spawn.py --prompt \\\"run pytest and report\\\" -- src/` \u2014 hook produces NO warning (false positive eliminated)\\n3. `ruff check src/` \u2014 hook produces warning (true positive preserved)\\n4. `uv run ruff check plugins/` \u2014 hook produces warning (true positive preserved)\\n5. `pytest tests/ -x` \u2014 hook produces warning (true positive preserved)\\n6. `uv run prek run --files src/foo.py` \u2014 hook produces warning (true positive preserved \u2014 `prek run` is not in quotes)\\n7. `uv run spawn.py spawn 'prek run --files foo.py'` \u2014 hook produces NO warning (false positive eliminated \u2014 `prek run` is inside a quoted argument)\\n8. All existing non-Bash tool calls and subagent sessions continue to produce no warning (existing bypass logic unchanged)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-diagnostic-command-gate.cjs` |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/prevent-bash-tool-misuse.cjs` (second hook, same pattern \u2014 may have same issue) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 single function change in one ~120-line CJS file. Strip quoted strings from the raw command string before the regex loop. No test infrastructure exists; acceptance criteria can be verified manually with inline test invocations or a small companion test script.\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\nIn `matchesDiagnosticCommand` (line 41\u201348 of `pre-tool-diagnostic-command-gate.cjs`), each `DIAGNOSTIC_PATTERNS` regex is matched against the entire raw `command` string, including content inside single-quoted and double-quoted arguments. Shell quoting is never stripped before matching.\\n\\nThe specific failure mode: `uv run spawn.py spawn --name x 'run ruff check on foo'` \u2014 the literal substring `ruff check` appears inside a single-quoted argument that forms a kage-bunshin prompt. The regex `/\\\\bruff\\\\s+check\\\\b/` matches it just as it would match `ruff check src/`.\\n\\nThe hook is located at: `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-diagnostic-command-gate.cjs`\\n\",\"digest\":\"935a282736b5e5af18dc8b098ac22fee901f1ef01d662891b76bf489019f94ed\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCudiw\"}"}